WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.275
A teaching slide should support an explanation rather than compete with it.

00:00:04.275 --> 00:00:11.044
One clear claim, a relevant diagram and a small example usually communicate more effectively than a dense copied paragraph.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:15.675
Speaker notes can preserve detail that does not need to occupy the screen.

00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:25.448
Use a sorted array and target, show the first middle comparison, show the retained half, show the next comparison, and explain the stopping condition.

00:00:25.448 --> 00:00:30.565
Keep the same array positions visually consistent so learners can follow what was eliminated.

00:00:31.565 --> 00:00:34.823
What is a useful reason to animate an explanation?

00:00:34.823 --> 00:00:38.805
Animation helps when it makes a meaningful change or sequence visible.
